  "summary": "The stile Umbertino is a 19th-century style of Renaissance Revival architecture in Italy, typical of the eclecticism of late 19th century architecture and decorative arts in Europe, which mixes decorative elements from various historical styles.",
  "description": "The stile Umbertino is a 19th-century style of Renaissance Revival architecture in Italy, typical of the eclecticism of late 19th century architecture and decorative arts in Europe, which mixes decorative elements from various historical styles.\n\nThe Umbertine style takes its name from King Umberto I, who reigned over the Kingdom of Italy from 1878 until 1900. The stile Umbertino includes architecture, furniture and other decorative arts. The stile Umbertino was most popular in Rome.",
